    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0026",
      "sequence": 38,
      "meaning": "By the name’s grace, imperishable Śiva’s inauspicious attire becomes a treasury of auspiciousness. By the name’s grace, Śuka, Sanaka and the other accomplished sages and yogīs enjoy Brahman’s bliss. Nārada knew the name’s power: he is dear to the world and to Hari, while Hari is dear to him. Repeating the name, Prahlāda received the Lord’s grace and became the crown-jewel of devotees. Dhruva, stung by humiliation, repeated Hari’s name and gained an immovable, incomparable station. Remembering the purifying name, the Wind’s son brought Rāma under the sway of his devotion. The fallen Ajāmila, the elephant Gajendra and the courtesan became liberated through Hari’s name. How far can I tell the name’s greatness? Even Rāma cannot fully sing the name’s virtues. Rāma’s name is the wish-fulfilling tree and abode of welfare in Kali; by remembering it, Tulsī was transformed from hemp-like worthlessness into Tulsīdāsa, the holy basil’s servant.",
