    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0027",
      "sequence": 39,
      "meaning": "In all four ages, all three times and all three worlds, beings have become free of sorrow by repeating the name. Veda, Purāṇa and saints agree that love for Rāma is the fruit of every meritorious deed. In the first age meditation was the way, in the second sacrifice, and in Dvāpara worship pleased the Lord. Kali alone is impure and the root of stain; people’s minds are fish in an ocean of sin. In this terrible age the name is the wish-fulfilling tree: remembering it calms the whole world’s torments. In Kali, Rāma’s name grants what is cherished and acts as father and mother, serving welfare in this world and the next. In Kali there is neither effective ritual, devotion nor discernment; Rāma’s name is the one support. Kali is the deceit-filled Kālanemi, and the name is mighty Hanumān joined with right understanding. Rāma’s name is Narasiṃha and the age of Kali Hiraṇyakaśipu; the person who repeats it is like Prahlāda, whom that lion of the gods will protect after crushing the demon.",
